; Parse a direction or an adverb (word classes 2 and 0)
;
; The handler of class 2 (north, up, down, ne...) in ActionTable; class 0
; (adverbs such as "carefully", "please") enters at #R$76F2.
; .
; A direction that comes while the phrase still needs its command word
; (PF_NEED_COMMAND) is a command by itself, "north": it goes to the verb handler (#R$7731).
; Otherwise the word is the command's second word, which may be given once
; (PF_DIRECTION_OK): after a verb, or after an adverb ("go north", "take
; carefully"). After the nouns of EXCEPT the parser first returns to the main
; record (#R$7858). The word is stored as the record's second command word (+2,
; REC_WORD2) and parsing goes on with the next word. A second one, or one in
; a phrase that has already used it, is refused with "What ?" (#R$7929).
; .
; BC The word (dictionary offset)
; D Class of this word (set to 0 for a direction)
; E Parser flags (see #R$7585)
; IY Phrase record being built
@label=ParseDirection
@isub=BIT PF_NEED_COMMAND,E
c$76EC BIT 1,E       ;
 $76EE JR NZ,$7731   ; no command word yet: "north" is the command
 $76F0 LD D,$00      ;
; Entry point for the words of class 0.
@label=ParseAdverb
@isub=BIT PF_DIRECTION_OK,E
*$76F2 BIT 2,E       ;
 $76F4 JP Z,$7929    ; already used: RejectLine
 $76F7 LD A,($B719)  ; AllStage
@isub=CP ALL_STATE_EXCEPT
 $76FA CP $02        ;
 $76FC JR NZ,$7701   ;
 $76FE CALL $7858    ; PreviousRecord: back to the main record
@isub=RES PF_DIRECTION_OK,E
*$7701 RES 2,E       ; the second word is taken
@isub=LD L,REC_WORD2
 $7703 LD L,$02      ;
 $7705 CALL $7918    ; StoreRecordWord: second command word
 $7708 JP $75B4      ; ParseNextWord
